0..81 Comment "// The folds over a polymorphic list — its length, appending and mapping — in"
82..157 Comment "// the spellings an arm admits, each as the sugared form writes it: a `run`"
158..235 Comment "// that only sequences a call, its result returned or the `return` elided, is"
236..311 Comment "// written with the call nested in the constructor it returns. A structural"
312..385 Comment "// recursive call stands one stage below the list it was read from (Abel,"
386..461 Comment "// _Termination checking with types_, doi:10.1051/ita:2004015); the list is"
462..534 Comment "// the polymorphic one of Martin-Löf\'s type theory. A fold may take the"
535..610 Comment "// element type implicitly, `@[a : Type]`: its recursive call omits `a` and"
611..668 Comment "// passes the function\'s own. They run at the naturals in"
669..700 Comment "// `recursive-nat-lists.gandr`."
702..732 Comment "// The naturals and the lists."
